WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.549 --> 00:00:04.882
(hollering)

00:00:06.331 --> 00:00:07.164
- Dinner!

00:00:09.828 --> 00:00:12.161
(hollering)

00:00:14.808 --> 00:00:17.141
(hollering)

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.451
- My name is Tony Peacock.

00:00:32.451 --> 00:00:33.820
- Robby Goodman.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.220
- My name is Sheila
Frye, I am a ten time--

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.053
- Six time--

00:00:37.053 --> 00:00:39.780
- Two time champ of the
National Hollerin' Contest

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.090
of Spivey's Corner North Carolina.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.406
- Hollerin' is a controlled sound

00:00:44.406 --> 00:00:47.920
that farmers used to communicate

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.100
with one another before
they had modern conveniences

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.884
like electricity or telephones.

00:00:54.884 --> 00:00:57.964
(hollering)

00:00:57.964 --> 00:01:00.501
Hollerers had a certain rhythm,

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:04.390
and a modulation that would create an echo

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.140
that would travel over a long distance.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.450
(hollering)

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.695
But there isn't just one type of holler.

00:01:12.695 --> 00:01:15.227
- There are actually
four types of hollers.

00:01:15.227 --> 00:01:18.512
Number one: functional—
it serves a purpose.

00:01:18.512 --> 00:01:20.170
(hollering)

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.810
Such as calling down to a field,

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.700
or calling up from a field
when you needed something.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.430
Number two: communicative.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.740
(hollering)

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:29.942
You're communicating a message,

00:01:29.942 --> 00:01:32.780
such as good morning, good evening.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.233
Number three: distress.

00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:36.240
(hollering)

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.803
You need help.

00:01:37.803 --> 00:01:41.069
Number four: expressive—
just for sheer fun.

00:01:41.069 --> 00:01:43.020
(hollering)

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.943
Many times that could be in
the form of tunes or ditties.

00:01:45.943 --> 00:01:48.030
(hollering)

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.100
These types of hollers were
what the judges were looking for

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.923
at the National Hollerin' Contest.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:58.487
- The first ever National
Hollerin' Contest was in 1969.

00:01:58.487 --> 00:02:01.790
It was started to raise funds for

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:05.991
the local fire department,
it became a nationwide hit.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:10.991
Hey, that's me, I won the
junior division in 1978,

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.530
my holler was a distress holler,

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.515
and it sounded like a siren.

00:02:15.515 --> 00:02:17.135
- And I'm proud to be a winner.

00:02:17.135 --> 00:02:20.480
- Everybody had their own
twist that they put on it.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.080
The National Hollerin' Contest ran

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:26.389
for about 48 years till 2015.

00:02:26.389 --> 00:02:30.630
We created the World
Wide Hollerin' Festival

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.290
that's located in Hope
Mills to try to preserve

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.283
and keep the tradition of hollerin’ alive.

00:02:39.111 --> 00:02:42.830
- Hollerin' is an important
piece of culture in this region

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:47.250
because it helps us remember our past.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.720
We can also appreciate the

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.940
modern conveniences we have today.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.050
- Hollerin' is part of simpler times,

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:55.680
and it's just something
that we need to treasure

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.980
because we need to know our history.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:00.935
- I love hollering cause it
brings the community together,

00:03:00.935 --> 00:03:05.423
and just the fellowship that
you have with one another.

00:03:05.423 --> 00:03:07.914
We want to keep that tradition alive.

00:03:07.914 --> 00:03:10.331
(soft music)

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.957
(ping)

